    <!-- Opt out of the macOS 26 "Liquid Glass" redesign (applies to AppKit/SwiftUI
         despite the UI prefix). Which design the app gets depends on the SDK it was
         built against: macOS 26 SDK builds (Xcode 26, locally and in CI) get the new
         floating rounded sidebar panel, older-SDK builds keep the classic flush
         sidebar — so the layout flip-flopped between build machines. This key pins
         the classic pre-Tahoe design regardless of build SDK; macOS before 26
         ignores it. Apple guarantees the key for ONE major release only: before
         macOS 27 the app must deliberately adopt the new design, then remove it. -->
    <key>UIDesignRequiresCompatibility</key>
    <true/>
